{"book":20,"chapter":31,"context":{"chapter":31,"title":"The Woman of Strength","summary":"King Lemuel records his mother's advice: avoid wasting strength on women and wine, and speak up for the voiceless. The book closes with an alphabetical poem praising a capable, God-fearing wife.","background":"Lemuel is otherwise unknown and may, like Agur, come from Massa. Verses 10–31 form an acrostic: each of the 22 verses begins with the next letter of the Hebrew alphabet. 'Virtuous woman' is literally 'woman of strength' or worth, the phrase Boaz uses of Ruth (Ruth 3:11).","customs":[{"term":"Spindle and distaff","verses":"31:19","note":"Hand-spinning tools: the distaff held raw wool or flax, and the spindle twisted it into thread."},{"term":"Known in the gates","verses":"31:23","note":"Elders sat at the city gate to settle disputes and conduct public business."}],"watchFor":["The book's last teacher is a king's mother (vv. 1–9).","Her fear of the Lord (v. 30) echoes 1:7, so the book begins and ends there.","Many readers see her as wisdom lived out, matching Lady Wisdom in chapters 1–9."],"connections":["Ruth 3:11","Proverbs 12:4","Proverbs 1:7","1 Peter 3:3-4"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["דִּבְרֵי","divrei","H1697","HNcmpc","[the] words of"],["לְמוּאֵל","lemu'el","H3927","HNpm","Lemuel"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king"],["מַשָּׂא","masa'","H4853","HNcbsa","an oracle"],["אֲשֶׁר","'asher-","H834","HTr","which"],["יִסְּרַתּוּ","yiseratu","H3256","HVpp3fs/Sp3ms","she instructed him"],["אִמּוֹ","'imo","H517","HNcfsc/Sp3ms","mother his"]],"x":[[20006020,20006020,7],[20001008,20001008,6],[55001005,55001005,6],[55003015,55003015,3]],"xn":4},"2":{"w":[["מַה","mah-","H4100","HPi","what?"],["בְּרִי","beri","H1121","HNcmsc/Sp1bs","O son my"],["וּמַה","umah-","H4100","HC/Pi","and what?"],["בַּר","bar-","H1121","HNcmsc","O son of"],["בִּטְנִי","bitni","H990","HNcfsc/Sp1bs","womb my"],["וּמֶה","umeh","H4100","HC/Pi","and what?"],["בַּר","bar-","H1121","HNcmsc","O son of"],[